WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.610
Better learning design begins with performance.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.780
What should learners be able to do after the course that they could not do reliably

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.320
before?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.070
Once that outcome is clear, the objective, examples, practice, feedback,

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.310
and assessment can all point in the same direction.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.230
If the goal is decision quality, the course should include decisions.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.690
If the goal is procedure accuracy, the course should include procedural practice.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:22.325
If the goal is judgment, the course should expose learners to realistic tradeoffs.

00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:23.445
Sequencing matters.

00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:27.100
Learners often benefit from concrete examples before abstract rules,

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.470
simple cases before complex ones, and guided practice before independent performance.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.900
Summaries and reflection help learners consolidate what they noticed and connect it to

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.695
future use.

00:00:35.695 --> 00:00:38.705
Feedback loops help them improve while there is still time to adjust.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:42.680
Assessment alignment keeps the course honest by measuring the capability the instruction

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.750
was supposed to build.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.800
Good design also avoids information dumps.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.315
More content is not automatically more learning.

00:00:48.315 --> 00:00:51.840
A course can be comprehensive and still be structured, focused, and usable.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.080
Inclusive and accessible design strengthens learning by reducing unnecessary barriers and

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.850
making participation more reliable across different learners and environments.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.480
The aim is not passive completion.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.155
The aim is to create conditions where people can build durable understanding and usable

00:01:05.155 --> 00:01:05.610
skill.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.100
This does not require every course to be elaborate.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.085
Even a short module can be stronger when it states a performance goal,

00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:14.520
uses a concrete example, asks learners to retrieve or apply the idea,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.760
and gives feedback that points to improvement.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.950
The discipline is to spend course time on the things most likely to change what the

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.600
learner can do afterward.
